source: crates/trousseau-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Command-line interface for the trousseau encrypted keyring.

Usage: trousseau [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init         Create a new store
  info         Show information about the resolved store
  set          Set a key's value
  get          Get a key's value
  ls           List keys
  rm           Remove one or more keys
  mv           Rename a key
  recipients   Manage a recipients store's recipient list
  rekey        Re-encrypt the store, optionally changing its kind or recipients
  export       Export the store's entries
  import       Import entries into the store
  run          Run a command with the store's entries injected as environment variables
  env          Print the store's entries as environment variable assignments
  edit         Edit the store in `$VISUAL` or `$EDITOR`
  migrate      Migrate a legacy v0.4 store into a new store
  completions  Print a shell completion script
  man          Print a roff man page
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Global options:
      --store <PATH>            Use this store file. Wins over `--global` and over store discovery
                                [env: TROUSSEAU_STORE=]
      --global                  Use your personal store instead of the nearest project store (the
                                `.trousseau` file in this directory or a parent)
      --identity <PATH>         An identity (private key) file to try when unlocking. Repeatable.
                                Also tried: `TROUSSEAU_IDENTITY_FILE`, the config file's
                                `identity.files`, the default identity file, `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` and
                                `~/.ssh/id_rsa`
      --passphrase-file <PATH>  Read the store's passphrase from this file instead of prompting. One
                                trailing newline is stripped
      --json                    Print one JSON document on stdout instead of text. Errors become a
                                JSON object on stderr
      --quiet                   Suppress informational messages on stderr. Errors still print
      --no-input                Never prompt. A command that would prompt fails instead: exit 4 for
                                a secret, exit 2 for a confirmation
